    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Synthesize speech for a text segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --text TEXT         TTS text content (required)\r\n          --speed TEXT        Playback / synthesis speed, e.g. 1.0\r\n          --speaker TEXT      TTS voice speaker id recognized by the TTS service (e.g. SAMI\r\n                              voice_type BV001_fast_streaming), not a display name or resource\r\n                              id\r\n          --audio-path TEXT   Existing/generated tone audio path\r\n          --resource-id TEXT  Tone/voice material resource id\r\n          --network-mode TEXT Network adapter mode, e.g. real / mock / offline\r\n          --output-dir TEXT   Directory for generated audio output\r\n          --audio-format TEXT Generated audio format, e.g. wav / mp3\r\n          --write-to-draft TEXT \r\n                              Write generated audio into the draft: true / false\r\n          --copy-to-draft TEXT \r\n                              Copy generated audio into the draft workspace: true / false\r\n          --start-time <microseconds> \r\n                              Target timeline start in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --duration <microseconds> \r\n                              Target duration in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --source-start-time <microseconds> \r\n                              Source audio start in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --source-duration <microseconds> \r\n                              Source audio duration in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --target-track-index TEXT \r\n                              Target audio track index\r\n          --replace TEXT      Replace existing text-reading audio bound to the target: true /\r\n                              false\r\n          --provider-params-json TEXT \r\n                              Provider-specific parameters as a JSON object or @path\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Synthesize speech from text at normal speed\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo tts --text \"Hello world\" --speed 1.0 --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Pick a specific TTS voice speaker id\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo tts --text \"Hello world\" --speaker BV001_fast_streaming --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Use the curl network adapter with provider params for dev verification\r\n  $ LYRA_ALGO_NETWORK_ADAPTER=curl lyra-cli draft algo tts --text \"Hello world\" --provider-params-json '{\"tone_type\":\"BV001\",\"volume\":1.0}' --seg-id <UUID>\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - TTS auth and network access default to placeholder adapters.\r\n  - Set LYRA_TTS_COOKIE or LYRA_TTS_HEADERS_JSON for dev curl verification.\r\n",
